The trap 500 teams will fall into

Every team reading this PS sees the same surface requirements: "form → calculate → PDF → dashboard." With 500 teams on one statement, the demos will converge hard — a React form, a few hardcoded pass/fail checks, a jsPDF export, done. Judges will see this pattern 400+ times in one day. That sameness is actually your opening: the PS rewards domain correctness and legal defensibility, and almost nobody will do the actual metrology homework. I did some of it below so you're not guessing.

What the PS is actually testing (domain research)

OIML R76 is two documents, not one — most teams won't know this:

R76-1 — the metrological/technical requirements (what "pass" means)
R76-2 — the actual prescribed test report format: General information about the type → test equipment info → Summary of type evaluation → 1) Weighing performance → 2) Temperature effect on no-load indication → 3) Eccentricity (using weights / rolling load) → 4) Discrimination & sensitivity → 5) Repeatability → 6) Time-dependence, and onward through stability of equilibrium, tilting, tare, warm-up, voltage variation, temperature/damp-heat testsThis is the OIML R 76-2 test report format, covering general information about the type, information about test equipment, a summary of type evaluation, and numbered sections for weighing performance, temperature effect on no-load indication, eccentricity (using weights and using a rolling load), discrimination and sensitivity, and repeatability. The full Annex A test battery also includes eccentricity, discrimination and sensitivity, repeatability, time dependence, stability of equilibrium, tilting, tare, warm-up test, voltage variation, and temperature test. 
