The Indian regulatory ecosystem you're plugging into (this is where you win on legitimacy):

Model approval testing is done only by RRSLs or NABL-accredited laboratories recognized under the Legal Metrology (Approval of Models) Rules, 2011 — a laboratory seeking recognition must have adequate measuring equipment, qualified staff, a proper recording system, and NABL accreditation in the relevant field. This gives you your role hierarchy for free: Lab Technician (data entry) → Principal Officer/Lab In-Charge (review) → Director, Legal Metrology (approval) — map "role-based permissions" onto this real chain instead of inventing generic Admin/User roles. 
